AB  - Aim
The aim of this study was to determine the ChatGPT experiences of Master of Science (MSc) (n = 10) and Doctor of Philosophy in Nursing (PhD) (n = 5) students in the field of public health nursing.
Background
ChatGPT has become an important support tool in the fields of education and research with rapidly developing artificial intelligence technology and its potential applications are increasingly relevant in public health nursing education.
Design
Study was designed as a descriptive qualitative study.
Method
This study was conducted with master’s and doctoral students in the field of public health nursing at a university. Purposive sampling method and semi-structured interviews were used in the study.
Results
The themes of “its role in public health nursing, concerns about its use, benefits, future predictions” and sub-themes were created. Students highlighted it as an effective tool in both academic and daily contexts but also expressed concerns about its usage. These findings underline its dual role as both a supportive and challenging innovation in the field of public health nursing education.
Conclusion
The results of the study can contribute to the development of educational programs by determining the concerns, benefits and future expectations of students in the process of using ChatGPT, thereby providing one of the first empirical perspectives in the context of public health nursing education.
